@IngestionService_HostAddress = http://localhost:5500
@AuthService_HostAddress = http://localhost:5300

### Log in first — the retrieval endpoints require a bearer token.
# @name login
POST {{AuthService_HostAddress}}/auth/v1/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@proptrack.local",
  "password": "ChangeMe123!"
}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### Semantic search — top-k chunks by cosine similarity (dealId/documentId optional filters)
POST {{IngestionService_HostAddress}}/ingestion/v1/search
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "were any environmental conditions identified?",
  "dealId": "e06e3cce-2188-432b-9d9c-1ecaf62c6db2",
  "topK": 5
}

### Search scoped to a single document
POST {{IngestionService_HostAddress}}/ingestion/v1/search
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "asking price and due diligence period",
  "documentId": "REPLACE_WITH_DOCUMENT_ID",
  "topK": 3
}

### Hybrid — pgvector + OpenSearch BM25, fused with RRF
# `mode` is dense | lexical | hybrid; omitted, SEARCH_MODE decides. `score` is cosine in
# every mode (back-filled for chunks only BM25 found), so the ai-service floors keep
# working; `rank` carries the fused order, `lexScore`/`fusedScore` are diagnostic.
POST {{IngestionService_HostAddress}}/ingestion/v1/search
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "What is the assessor parcel number?",
  "dealId": "e06e3cce-2188-432b-9d9c-1ecaf62c6db2",
  "topK": 8,
  "mode": "hybrid",
  "rrfK": 10
}

### Lexical only — BM25 with no vector component
# Useful for seeing what fusion is being handed. Exact tokens (APNs, "$67,834,000",
# "6.69%") rank far better here than in dense; paraphrased questions rank far worse.
POST {{IngestionService_HostAddress}}/ingestion/v1/search
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "What is the assessor parcel number?",
  "dealId": "e06e3cce-2188-432b-9d9c-1ecaf62c6db2",
  "topK": 8,
  "mode": "lexical"
}

### Off-domain probe under hybrid — the abstention guard rail
# BM25 WILL return chunks here (the tokens occur in the corpus). They must still come back
# with cosine ~0.07, which is what ai-service's MinScore=0.15 rejects. If these ever
# arrive with a high `score`, the fused score has leaked into the wrong field.
POST {{IngestionService_HostAddress}}/ingestion/v1/search
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "What is the best recipe for sourdough bread?",
  "dealId": "e06e3cce-2188-432b-9d9c-1ecaf62c6db2",
  "topK": 8,
  "mode": "hybrid"
}

### Lexical index status — pre-flight before trusting any hybrid measurement
# inSync=false means the backfill has not run, or a dual-write failed:
#   docker compose exec ingestion-service python -m app.backfill --repair
GET {{IngestionService_HostAddress}}/ingestion/v1/lexical/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Parsed markdown artifact for a document (what ai-service will summarise from)
GET {{IngestionService_HostAddress}}/ingestion/v1/documents/REPLACE_WITH_DOCUMENT_ID/parsed
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Health — DB + LiteLLM reachability (no auth)
GET {{IngestionService_HostAddress}}/health
